{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And now, behold, I go to my people; come, let me advise you.</b> I will give you counsel that you may cause them to stumble — namely, that he declared the daughters of Moab permitted to the children of Israel, because he knew that their Elohim hates licentiousness. And what is stated here in general terms is explained in another place, namely where it says (Numbers 31:16): ״הן הנה היו לבני ישראל בדבר בלעם״ and so forth." "<b>What this people shall do.</b> That is, I will advise you and tell you what this people shall do to your people at the end of days — namely what it says, ״ומחץ פאתי מואב״; but now you have no cause to fear them, for they will do you no harm." "<b>And the Ramban,</b> of blessed memory, wrote: איעצך ואגיד לך — I will advise you and tell you counsel ordained from before HaShem, אשר יעשה העם הזה לעמך באחרית הימים — what this people shall do to your people at the end of days. And He revealed to him this prophecy, that his people would not fall into the hand of Israel now, but only at the end of days. Now there were four prophecies: the first is what he said — that Israel is HaShem's portion and inheritance, that they are ״עם לבדד ישכון ובגוים לא נתחשב״; the second, he prophesied concerning the conquest of the land and that they would slay the mighty kings therein, as it is written: ״הן עם כלביא יקום״ and so forth; the third, he saw their dwelling in the land in rest and tranquility, and said: ״מה טובו אוהליך יעקב״ — and that they would raise up a king who would defeat Agag and that the yoke of kingship would be exalted, so that he saw David exalted on high, as it is said (2 Samuel 5:12): ״וידע דוד כי הכינו ה׳ למלך״; and now, in this fourth prophecy, he added to see the matter of the Messiah, and therefore he extended the matter very far, saying ״אראנו ולא עתה אשורנו ולא קרוב״ — which he did not say in any of the earlier prophecies. And he said that this is the counsel that HaShem advised concerning the end of days. And he called himself now ״שומע אמרי אל ומחזה שדי״ — he sees, just as he did in the third prophecy, and he added to call himself ״יודע דעת עליון״. And one who says thus, יודע דעת עליון — 'knowing the knowledge of the Most High' — means to say that he knows what is in the mind of El Elyon to do in His world at the end of days; and this is in the manner of what is said (Isaiah 63:4): ״כי יום נקם בלבבי״. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: 'to the mouth it was not revealed' (לבא לפומא לא גליא). End of quote." "<b>And since</b> the hidden matter is concealed in the heart, therefore the hidden Name is called 'heart' (לב), as it is written (Psalms 73:26): ״צור לבבי וחלקי אלהים לעולם״. And the angels, who are His emissaries, are called His mouth, for they are dispatched to the prophets to tell them the things to come. If so, the prophets are the mouth of the angels, and the angels are the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He — and He is לבא לפומא (the heart that does not reach the mouth), for the Holy One, blessed be He, did not reveal the End even to the angels, all the more so to the prophets. And Daniel did not know it, but it was said to him (Daniel 12:9): ״כי סתומים וחתומים הדברים עד עת קץ״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:59.842575049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}